    "within": "Questions 1 to 2 ask what goes with 0, then 5, to make 5, on the sum line only. Question 3 matches number words to parts. Question 4 is the sum line for what goes with 3 to make 5. Question 5 taps six tiles with no dots to make 5. Question 6 puts 1 and 4 together in pictures. Question 7 is reverse order for what goes with 2 to make 5. Question 8 is the sum line for a hidden part: what goes with 2 to make 5. Question 9 matches other ways to make 3, 4 and 5. Question 10 picks another pair that makes 5. No hints.",
    "versus": "Easy is small sums from 2 up to 5, or four tiles with dots. Medium is 4 and 5 with 0 and 5, and may use six tiles. Hard stays on 5, uses 0, reverse order, number words, a hidden part, and tiles with no dots. Same node: composition of each number to 5."
